description: Standards for frontend coding
alwaysApply: false
---

# Styling & Components

- Use ONLY Tailwind utility classes for layout and spacing
- Use Shadcn UI components for interactive elements (buttons, forms, cards, etc.)
- Never write custom CSS—no inline styles or CSS files
- Use configured typography scale and semantic theme from globals.css
- Use '@tabler/icons-react' for icons; fallback to lucide-react if icon not available
- Ensure responsive design with Tailwind breakpoints (sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl)

# Shadcn UI

- Always use Shadcn components when appropriate (Button, Card, Input, Form, etc.)
- Before using component, check if it was installed: `npx shadcn@latest list`
- If not installed, install as needed: `npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]`
- Import from @/components/ui/[component-name]
- Use Shadcn's built-in variants (default, secondary, destructive, outline, ghost, link)
- Extend variants in component files if needed; document custom variants in component comments

# Next.js & React

- Prefer Server Components (no 'use client' unless needed for interactivity or hooks)
- Use route groups `(public)`, `(protected)`, `(auth)`, `admin/` for logical organization
- Dynamic routes use `[param]` naming convention
- Client components marked with `'use client'` at top of file

# Database & API

- Always call `connectDB()` in API routes (it's idempotent)
- Use `.lean()` when serializing Mongoose documents to JSON for performance
- Keep model methods static where possible (e.g., Assessment.calculateResult())
- API responses should be strongly typed with TypeScript interfaces (not just Zod validation)
- Store guest/temporary state in `sessionStorage` for form data persistence

# Forms & Validation

- Use React Hook Form + Zod for all forms
- Validate on both client and server
- Type form inputs based on Zod schema inferred types

# Design-to-Code Workflow (MCP)

- When provided a Penpot URL, ALWAYS use the Penpot MCP tools to inspect the design before writing code
- Extract design tokens (colors, spacing, typography) from Penpot and map to globals.css variables or Tailwind config

# Error Handling

- Add error boundaries with error.tsx in route groups for graceful error UI
- API routes: Always validate input with Zod, respond with `{ error: string }` on validation failure
- Client components: Use try/catch for fetch calls, display user-friendly error messages
- Database operations: Ensure connectDB() is called; handle connection errors gracefully

# TypeScript & Coding Standards

- Strict TypeScript mode enabled (tsconfig.json)
- Use TypeScript for all components and utility functions
- If a component requires state, use functional components with React Hooks
- No `any` types—infer or define types explicitly
- For complex layouts, prioritize CSS Grid/Flexbox as defined in design files

# Architecture Patterns

- **Protected Routes**: Place in `(protected)/` group (auth middleware exists in /src/lib/auth)
- **Admin Routes**: Place in `admin/` group with admin role checks
- **Server vs Client**: RSC for data fetching/validation; pass serialized data to client components
- **Questions & Scoring**: Refer to Assessment model for static scoring logic; don't duplicate calculations

# Do NOT

- Add comments explaining obvious code (self-documenting code only)
- Add features not requested or mentioned by user
- Use external libraries beyond what's installed: Next.js, Tailwind, Shadcn, Tabler Icons, Lucide React, React Hook Form, Zod
- Use raw hex code or pixel measurements for styling—always use Tailwind classes or design tokens
- Create additional components unless explicitly requested
- Hallucinate design properties; if Penpot value is missing, ask user or use closest Tailwind equivalent
